# {{instance_name}}-data

A **registry** instance tended by the kestrel engine: records of a corpus
kestrel tends, each carrying a source and a `last_verified` date, with an
append-only changelog. This repo is the data; a paired site repo (once
created via `/instantiate-site`) is the rendered surface; the engine is the
machinery. `kestrel.yaml` at this root is the instance manifest
(`kind: registry`).

Scaffolded by kestrel's `/instantiate-data` meta-skill (ROADMAP/KITS.md
§3/§5) from `library/scaffolds/data-registry/`. Next steps, in order:

1. Populate `kestrel.yaml`'s `sources:`, `cadence:`, and `outputs:` blocks
   (all left as placeholder comments here).
2. Replace `schema/record.yaml`'s DRAFT stub with this instance's own
   record shape once its domain research has actually landed — do not
   finalize it before then.
3. Run the engine's kit installer against this repo to bring in this
   instance's operating skills (`/tend`, `/curate`, `/verify`, `/publish`)
   and agent docs (`/instantiate-data`'s last step does this automatically;
   re-run it later via `/install-kit` after any library update).
4. Confirm this instance is registered in kestrel's own `instances.yaml`
   (the session running `/instantiate-data` shows the exact block to add
   and appends/commits it separately, in kestrel).

**Never:** edit `records/` outside `/curate`'s mechanics · modify an
existing `changelog/` entry after it's written (append-only) · let an
LLM-edited YAML file go unvalidated (`yaml.safe_load` or revert).
